# Walkthrough - Compliance and Login Restructuring

I have restructured the compliance reporting features to separate high-level status from detailed logs. The Login page now serves as the high-level compliance dashboard for unauthenticated users, while the Compliance page within the app focuses on the formal Base Year Recalculation Log.

## Changes

### 1. Compliance Page ([compliance.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/compliance.html))
- **Visuals Removed**: Removed the 3 "Status Cards" (EPA, ISO, GHG Protocol) and the detailed "Gap Analysis" checklist.
- **Header Updated**: Renamed from "Regulatory Compliance & Standards" to **"Base Year Recalculation History"**.
- **Focus**: The page is now dedicated solely to tracking base year recalculations (ISO 14064-1 requirement).

### 2. Login Page ([index.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/index.html))
- **New Visuals**: Added the 3 Compliance Status Cards to the left-hand branding panel.
- **Styling**: Adapted the card styles to blend with the login page's Teal (`#1a5d4a`) theme using semi-transparent backgrounds.
- **Content**:
    - **EPA 40 CFR Part 98**: 100% Score.
    - **ISO 14064**: 100% Score.
    - **GHG Protocol**: 100% Score.

## Verification Results

### Manual Code Verification
- Checked [compliance.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/compliance.html) to ensure the previous large grid of cards is gone and the table remains accessible.
- Checked [index.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/index.html) to confirm the new `.compliance-grid-login` class is present and contains the 3 cards.
- Verified CSS in [index.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/index.html) head for `status-card` looks correct for the dark teal theme.

### Visual Consistency
The Login page now immediately communicates the platform's robust compliance status to prospective or returning users, reinforcing trust before they even sign in.
